{"parents":[{"StatuteId":2048328,"Type":"Title","Statute":"23A"},{"StatuteId":2048996,"Type":"Chapter","Statute":"30"}],"Previous":"23A-29-2","Next":"23A-30-1","StatuteId":2048996,"Statute":"23A-30","Type":"Chapter","CatchLine":"(RULE 34) ARREST OF JUDGMENT ","FilePath":null,"FileName":null,"Htmlpath":null,"Htmlfilename":null,"Title":23,"TitleLetter":"A","Chapter":30,"ChapterLetter":null,"Section":0,"SubSec":0,"SubSection":null,"Word":null,"Html":"                                                                   \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n                                                                          \r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<html>\r\n<head>\r\n<title>23A-30 (RULE 34) ARREST OF JUDGMENT </title>\r\n<meta name=\"Keywords\" content=\"South Dakota Codified Laws SDCL 23A-30 (RULE 34) ARREST OF JUDGMENT \">\r\n<meta name=\"Description\" content=\"South Dakota Codified Laws 23A-30\">\r\n</head>\r\n<body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\">\r\n\r\n<!-- File converted by Wp2Html Version 4.0  -->\r\n<!-- Email Andrew@brackenbeds.co.uk for more details  -->\r\n\r\n<!-- WP Style Open: System_34 --><!-- WP Style End: System_34 -->\r\n<div align=\"full\">\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style On: HG4 --><div align=\"center\"><!-- WP Style End: HG4 -->\r\nCHAPTER 23A-30\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style Off: HG4 --><!-- WP Style End: HG4 -->\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style On: HG4C --><div align=\"center\"><!-- WP Style End: HG4C -->\r\n(RULE 34) ARREST OF JUDGMENT\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style Off: HG4C --><!-- WP Style End: HG4C -->\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style On: B --><!-- WP Style End: B -->\r\n<a href=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=23A-30-1\">23A-30-1</a>\r\n<!-- WP Style Open: IN -->&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<!-- WP Style End: IN -->\r\n(Rule 34) Grounds for arrest of judgment--Time for motion.\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style Off: B --><!-- WP Style End: B -->\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style On: B --><!-- WP Style End: B -->\r\n<a href=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=23A-30-2\">23A-30-2</a>\r\n<!-- WP Style Open: IN -->&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<!-- WP Style End: IN -->\r\nEffect of arrest of judgment.\r\n<!-- WP Paired Style Off: B --><!-- WP Style End: B -->\r\n<br>\r\n<a href=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=23A-30-3\">23A-30-3</a>\r\n<!-- WP Style Open: IN -->&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<!-- WP Style End: IN -->\r\nRecommitment or admission to bail after arrest of judgment--Discharge if evidence\r\ninsufficient.<p>\r\n</p></div></div></body>\r\n</html>\r\n<hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048993Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048993SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048993CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048993Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048993DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048993DefaultParagraphFont-000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048993000002 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048993SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048993SCL-000003 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048993Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-30-1\"><span class=\"s2048993SENU\">23A-30-1</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048993SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048993CL\">(Rule 34) Grounds for arrest of judgment--Time for motion.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048993Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048993DefaultParagraphFont\">A court shall arrest judgment if an indictment or information does not charge an offense or if the court does not have jurisdiction of the offense charged. Any party may move to arrest judgment, but such motion must be made within ten days after the verdict or finding of guilty or after a plea of guilty or nolo contendere, or within such further time as the court may fix during the ten</span><span class=\"s2048993DefaultParagraphFont-000001\">-</span><span class=\"s2048993DefaultParagraphFont\">day period.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048993Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048993000002\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048993Normal\"><span class=\"s2048993SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048993SCL-000003\"><span>  Supreme Court Rule 409, 1939; SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3677; SDCL, § 23-47-1; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 381.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048994Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048994SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048994CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048994Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048994DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048994000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048994SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048994SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048994Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-30-2\"><span class=\"s2048994SENU\">23A-30-2</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048994SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048994CL\">Effect of arrest of judgment.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048994Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048994DefaultParagraphFont\">The effect of allowing a motion in arrest of judgment is to place the defendant in the same situation in which he was before the indictment or information was filed.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048994Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048994000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048994Normal\"><span class=\"s2048994SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048994SCL-000002\"><span>  Supreme Court Rule 409, 1939; SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3677; SDCL, § 23-47-2; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 382.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html><hr><br><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><title></title><meta name=\"Generator\" content=\"PowerTools for Open XML\"><style>span { white-space: pre-wrap; }\r\np.s2048995Normal {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048995SENU {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048995CL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\np.s2048995Normal-000000 {\r\n    margin-top: 0;\r\n    margin-bottom: 0;\r\n    text-indent: 0.50in;\r\n    text-align: justify;\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    line-height: 108%;\r\n    margin-left: 0;\r\n    margin-right: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048995DefaultParagraphFont {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048995000001 {\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048995SCL {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: bold;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.s2048995SCL-000002 {\r\n    font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';\r\n    font-size: 12pt;\r\n    font-style: normal;\r\n    font-weight: normal;\r\n    margin: 0;\r\n    padding: 0;\r\n}\r\n</style></head><body><div style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif'; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1;\"><div><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048995Normal\"><a href=\"https://sdlegislature.gov/Statutes/Codified_Laws/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&amp;Statute=23A-30-3\"><span class=\"s2048995SENU\">23A-30-3</span></a><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048995SENU\">. </span><span class=\"s2048995CL\">Recommitment or admission to bail after arrest of judgment--Discharge if evidence insufficient.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048995Normal-000000\"><span class=\"s2048995DefaultParagraphFont\">If from the evidence introduced at a trial there is probable cause to believe a defendant is guilty, and a new indictment or information can be framed upon which he may be convicted, a court may order him to be recommitted to the officer of the proper county or admitted to bail anew to answer the new indictment or information. If there is probable cause to believe him guilty of another offense, he must be committed or held thereon. If no evidence appears sufficient to charge him with any offense, he must, if in custody, be discharged or, if admitted to bail, have his bail exonerated.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048995Normal\"><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048995000001\"> </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" class=\"s2048995Normal\"><span class=\"s2048995SCL\">Source:</span><span xml:space=\"preserve\" class=\"s2048995SCL-000002\"><span>  SDC 1939 &amp; Supp 1960, § 34.3678; SDCL, § 23-47-4; <a rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/SessionLaws/1978/178/null/null\" aria-label=\"SL 1978, ch 178\">SL 1978, ch 178</a>, § 383.</span></span></p></div></div></body></html></head></html>","Credits":null,"StatuteText":null,"Article":null,"Created":null,"CreatedById":null,"LastUpdated":null,"LastUpdatedBy":null,"Repealed":false,"StatuteReferencesReferencesStatute":[],"StatuteReferencesStatute":[]}